                <head>215. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The Migratory Labor agreement between Mexico and the United States, which entered
                    into force on August 11, 1951, was extended <pb facs="0732" n="698"
                        xml:id="pg698"/> to December 31, 1956, by exchange of notes between Mexican
                    Foreign Minister Padilla Nervo and Ambassador White on December 23 in Mexico City. For text of the Migratory
                    Labor agreement of August 11, 1951, see <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Treaties and Other International Agreements</hi> (UST) 1951, volume 2 (part
                    2), page 1940. For text of the notes extending the agreement, see 6 UST (pt. 5)
                    6058. Documentation on the subject is in Department of State, Central File
                    811.06(M).</p>
            </div>
